<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<xs:schema xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema"
	xmlns:vc="http://www.w3.org/2007/XMLSchema-versioning"
	vc:minVersion="1.1"
	elementFormDefault="qualified"
	xmlns:tns="http://www.lotar.org/schemas/mbse/p520#"
	xmlns:p500="http://www.lotar.org/schemas/mbse/p500#"
	targetNamespace="http://www.lotar.org/schemas/mbse/p520#"
	attributeFormDefault="unqualified">

	<xs:import namespace="http://www.lotar.org/schemas/mbse/p500#" schemaLocation="P500_Series_Common.xsd"/>

	<!--
		FMI-LS-ref import (moved from P515_SCHEMA.xsd, D-23, 2026-09-05; originally 2026-07-20)
		=========================================================================
		NOTE ON NAMESPACE STYLE: this schema deliberately declares no default namespace (see below).
		Vendored from modelica/fmi-ls-ref PR #36 (not yet merged upstream; wired in on the
		explicit instruction to execute the P515_FMI_LS_Ref_Plan.md plan assuming it merges;
		the xs:import->xs:include fix landed separately via PR #40, see T-29). This schema has
		no target namespace of its own, so no namespace= attribute is given here (matches how
		fmi3LayeredStandardReferenceManifest.xsd itself imports fmi3Annotation.xsd). Provides
		the TRelated/TLabel/fmiReferences definitions that P520_Related_Type (below) extends.

		CHANGED ON INTEGRATION (D-23): P515 kept a default namespace (xmlns="...p515#") and
		reset it with xmlns="" on P515_Related_Type so that base="TRelated" would reach the
		no-namespace type. That never compiled under xmlschema (it resolved the unprefixed name
		to the target namespace anyway), the "TRelated fails to resolve" gap recorded in
		xml_form_app's registry and HANDOVER.md. A chameleon <xs:include> was tried first and
		rejected: fmi3LayeredStandardReferenceManifest.xsd declares
		attributeFormDefault="qualified", so absorbing it into the p520 namespace would have
		made @source/@role/@checksum p520-qualified in instances, breaking the FMI-LS-ref
		attribute convention. Fix actually applied: this schema declares NO default namespace
		(only xmlns:tns for its own target namespace) and every reference to one of its own
		types is written tns:Foo, so the one unprefixed reference left, base="TRelated",
		resolves to the no-namespace type in every processor with no tricks. Verified
		2026-09-05: compiles under lxml.etree.XMLSchema AND xmlschema.XMLSchema11, and
		fixtures/lotar-p520-test-full-VALID.xml validates under both. No instance change:
		TRelated's attributes stay unqualified, exactly as in the former P515 fixtures.
	-->
	<xs:import schemaLocation="../schemas-vendored/fmi3LayeredStandardReferenceManifest.xsd"/>

	<xs:complexType name="P520_ManifestType">
